[
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "# Lab 5: Protect the Heat Limit with a Rule\n\n**Goal:** Lock down `config/#` so only authorised operators (and `root`) can change `config/heat_limit_c`.\n\n**What you will build:**\n- **`ProtectWeatherConfig` (Rule):** An access-control rule (`DEFINE RULE`) that allows `Publish` to `config/#` only if the user is in the `operators` group or is `root`, and denies everyone else.\n\n> **Licence note:** Custom RBAC / Topic ACL Rules require the **event trial licence** from the organisers (or a Growth / Enterprise licence). If your Broker is on **Community Edition**, you can still follow this lab as a read-along (see the bottom of this notebook)."
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 1. Activate the Event Licence\n\nOpen **Broker Settings** (click `root` at the top right) → **License** → **Activation code**, paste the `CFLX-…` code from the organisers, and click **Activate** (or run `-activateLicense CFLX-your-code` in **Command Console**).\n\n- The badge next to `root` at the top right changes from *Community* to your licence tier.\n- Under **Broker Settings → License → Features**, confirm **RBAC / Topic ACL** is ticked.\n- If your licence badge is already active at the top right, skip this step!"
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 2. Create Users and the `operators` Group\n\nA group is created automatically as soon as you add a user to it. Open **Command Console** (`root` at the top right) and send these three commands one by one:\n\n```\n-addUser alice alice-pass-123\n-addUserToGroup alice operators\n-addUser bob bob-pass-123\n```\n\nNow `alice` is in the `operators` group, while `bob` is a regular user outside the group."
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 3. Deploy the `ProtectWeatherConfig` Rule\n\n`PRIORITY 100` is the highest priority you can assign to a custom Rule (`0–99` are reserved for the Broker's built-in system rules). Click **▷ (Run Cell)** below — the Broker replies *Rule 'ProtectWeatherConfig' added successfully*."
 },
 {
  "kind": 2,
  "language": "lot",
  "value": "DEFINE RULE ProtectWeatherConfig WITH PRIORITY 100 FOR Publish TO TOPIC \"config/#\"\n    IF USER IN GROUP \"operators\" OR USER IS \"root\" THEN\n        ALLOW\n    ELSE\n        DENY"
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## Check It Worked\n\n1. **Connect as `bob`:** Click `root` at the top right → **Log out**. On the connection screen, click **⚙** next to *Weather station* → **Add user**, enter `bob` / `bob-pass-123`, tick **Default** on `bob`'s row, and click **Connect**. (The HUB opens in limited mode with *No SYS* at the top right and fewer dock icons — that is normal for a non-admin user.)\n2. **Try to change the limit as `bob`:** In **Data Viewer → Publish**, publish `5` (with **Retain** ON) to `config/heat_limit_c`. The HUB shows *Sent (delivery unconfirmed)* — MQTT drops unauthorized publishes silently without an error.\n3. **Switch back to `root`:** Log out, click the user chip (*bob*) next to **Connect**, select `root`, and click **Connect**. Check `config/heat_limit_c` in **Data Viewer**: it is **still `30`**! `bob` was denied.\n4. **Optional — test as `alice`:** Connect as `alice` / `alice-pass-123` and publish `5` to `config/heat_limit_c`. Because `alice` is in `operators`, her change succeeds! Remember to set `config/heat_limit_c` back to `30` (Retain ON) as `root` or `alice` afterwards.\n\n**Read-along (Community Edition):** Click ▷ on the Rule cell once anyway to see the Broker's response: *RBAC / Topic Access Control rules require a Growth or Enterprise license*. Without the Rule active, `bob`'s publish of `5` *is* accepted — set the limit back to `30` before moving on to Lab 6.\n\nDocs: [Rule syntax](https://docs.coreflux.org/latest/lot-language/rules/syntax) · [RBAC](https://docs.coreflux.org/latest/lot-language/rules/rbac)."
 }
]
